  "name": "Arbalest Mastery stacks carry across chained Witchbane casts up to ten",
  "contract": [
    "Arbalest Mastery 706240: \"Each subsequent shot of a Witchbane cast deals 15% more damage, up to a maximum of 150%.\" Its progress aura 706241 stacks to 10 (StackAmount 10, EffectBasePoints 14 / DieSides 1 = 15% per stack) and lasts 1200 ms (DurationIndex 509); each Witchbane shot 704342 is multiplied by 1 + 0.15 x stacks, then adds a stack and refreshes the timer. Mentor rulings D-148 and D-152 read the tooltip by the live logs: stacks carry across chained casts (a cast issued as the previous channel's last shot lands) and drop 1.2 s after the last shot. A Witchbane channel (800165, 3000 ms, 750 ms period, extra initial tick) delivers five shots (D-143). The reference is the talented hunter's own first shot (no stack, multiplier 1), read alone before the second shot of the first channel; ratios to it cancel armor and the caster's stats. The control Witch Hunter has the same talents without Arbalest Mastery: its channel shows that no progress is granted without the talent, and its unstacked mean is kept as a diagnostic snapshot only; both players carry +10000 ranged attack power so a shot deals several hundred points and per-hit integer truncation stays near 0.1% (at the bare level 60 fixture a 63-point shot truncated a channel by 1.1%); the band is 1%. Each dummy carries Blessed Resilience 33143 (aura 197 SPELL_AURA_MOD_ATTACKER_SPELL_AND_WEAPON_CRIT_CHANCE, EffectBasePoints -1001, 6000 ms), a precondition fixture renewed right after every cast, so no shot is a critical hit (asserted) and every channel total is deterministic. Expected sums of multipliers: a channel from no stack 1 + 1.15 + 1.3 + 1.45 + 1.6 = 6.5; the chained second channel (stacks 5 to 9) 5 + 0.15 x 35 = 10.25; the third and fourth channels (stacks 10) 2.5 per shot, 12.5 per channel. After the twentieth shot the aura holds 10 stacks with a refreshed timer, outlasts the channel end and is gone when read about 1.5 s after the last shot launched (expiry 1.2 s after it); a fifth cast after that starts again from no stack (6.5). Timing reads are candidate batch_sensitive."
  ],
